add('R3-21','One actual writable noncreature surface≤1square foot within60ft; willing holder if attended.','Printed concentration up to1minute, one trigger.','Automatic inscription; one explicitly selected finite payload at its trigger.','NEW choose one payload: alarm—ordinary audible chime≤6seconds; repulsion—the triggering creature makes STR save or is pushed5ft directly away from the glyph along a legal supported path, no damage; ward—the triggering willing creature receives+2AC against its next committed attack before the caster’s next regular start. Choose one trigger: first subsequent direct bodily creature touch of the marked surface, or first actually visible creature entry from outside into5ft of it. Initial inscription/contact never triggers it. The glyph has ordinary visual perception only in the entry mode; no hidden identity/moral filter. Consume before the one payload, retain original caster/DC/ownership, and release the glyph concentration after that payload resolves.',
'This is not stored spell access, a separate free casting, damage by name, permanent trap or Rune Carving item. No new payloadRP cost is added beyond its actual source casting because this finite minor payload is the spell’s chosen effect; no recharge/retrigger. The same actual anchor can move only with its real custody/geometry, with trigger history retained; full suppression misses events without queue. Alarm needs actual acoustics; repulsion stops before occupied/unsafe/blocked space without crushing. The ward uses normal flatAC/one-use arbitration and grants no different card’s ability.',
'A visible creature entering the five-foot sensor can spend a repulsion glyph once. If a wall or invisibility prevents its ordinary visual detection, there is no triggered attack or stored event waiting for later unsuppression.',numbers={'rangeFeet':60,'surfaceSquareFeet':1,'seconds':60,'uses':1,'triggerRadiusFeet':5,'alarmSeconds':6,'pushFeet':5,'wardAcBonus':2})
